.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt HMKTVM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmktvm
.Nd run the auction searches used for a virtual-machine host
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmktvm
.Op Ar hcli-flags ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr sh 1
wrapper.
It calls
.Pa ~/bin/hcli
three times with
.Fl p Cm market
and prints a label before each table.
.Ev HCLI
overrides that path.
Extra arguments are appended to every call.
Each call uses the cached auction list when it is still fresh.
.Pp
Each search passes
.Fl o Cm format=price ,
.Fl o Cm re=ECC ,
.Fl o Cm re=ENT ,
and
.Fl o Cm disk.count.min=2 .
.Pp
Both patterns must match.
.Pp
The three searches, in order:
.Bl -tag -width "2disk 8gb storage <=$72 >=128G ram" -compact
.It 2disk 8gb storage <=$50 >=64G ram
.Fl M Cm 64
.Fl o Cm disk.min=8000
.Fl o Cm price.max=50
.It 2disk 4gb storage <=$40 >=64G ram
.Fl M Cm 64
.Fl o Cm disk.min=4000
.Fl o Cm price.max=40
.It 2disk 8gb storage <=$72 >=128G ram
.Fl M Cm 128
.Fl o Cm disk.min=8000
.Fl o Cm price.max=72
.El
.Pp
The labels say dollars.
.Cm price.max
is the monthly price in euros.
.Cm disk.min
is total gigabytes, so 8000 is 8 TB in the old decimal unit.
.Fl M
is the RAM floor in gigabytes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the status of the last
.Xr hcli 1
call.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hcli 1 ,
.Xr hmktst 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm-picky 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Todd T. Fries Aq Mt todd@fries.net
